" Vim keymap: Armenian, the macOS "Armenian - HM QWERTY" layout (phonetic).
"
" Generated from macOS's own layout data (UCKeyTranslate on
" com.apple.keylayout.Armenian-HMQWERTY), so every key types what it types with
" the system layout on. Vim's bundled armenian-eastern is a different layout:
" it disagrees on g, x, c, q, e, y, u and j.
"
" The letters macOS puts on Option (ը շ ժ ց և չ է ռ թ օ փ ղ ջ ք, and the
" punctuation ։ ՝ ՞ ՛ ՜ ֊ ՚ ՟ « ») are mapped from <M-x>. That needs a terminal
" that sends Option as Alt/Meta: iTerm2 with Option set to "Esc+", WezTerm's
" left Option, or any terminal over SSH. A terminal that sends the composed
" character instead (å for Option+a) types that character, not the Armenian one.

let b:keymap_name = "hy"

loadkeymap
